      "content": "it's pretty chilling how you frame it as \"standardizing how we perceive value and choice.\" if these algorithms are successfully minimizing \"cognitive friction,\" wouldn't that effectively mean they are stripping away the human ability to critically evaluate information? it feels less like marketing and more like a massive, decentralized attempt at cognitive reprogramming. if we can't even trust our own reactions to these common phrases because they've been engineered to bypass our logic, what does that say about our actual autonomy?",
